# Who gets this workstation, read by .local/lib/machine-mode.sh.
# Format:  mode|runners|unity_slots|unity_burst|level
#   mode         the word you type and the chip shows
#   runners      pool runners on this host taking new jobs (the governor's slot pin)
#   unity_slots  local Unity runs always open (slots.sh)
#   unity_burst  more local Unity runs when the machine has room
#   level        how fast the fleet starts work, a row of the levels file; mid is the confs' own numbers.
#                No mode pauses dispatch; `agent-hold set dispatch` is the one full stop.
#
# File order is the order `machine-mode next` and the chip's click walk. The last row is the
# mode with nothing set, so it must stay what the machine does with no mode at all.

full|1|2|1|high
reserved|0|1|0|low
shared|0|2|0|mid
open|0|2|1|mid
